/Title (Avoids massive if-else or switch-case blocks that lead to unmaintainable code \("spaghetti code"\).Enforces the Open/Closed Principle \(OCP\). If a new business requirement emerges \(e.g., adding a "Dual-Factor Authentication" state\), engineers can insert a new state class without breaking or refactoring existing transaction workflows.Protects system integrity by natively blocking illegal operations \(e.g., calling dispenseCash\(\) while the machine is in an IdleState throws an error rather than executing\))
